Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:42:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 026/154] fix: make the guard name the profile it declined
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The guard stops the crash but leaves the cause unknown, and the cause is one
fact away: which profile, and of what type.

GetForProfile passes create=true, so null means the factory's ProfileSelections
declined this profile TYPE - not that the service was merely missing. Only two
types are unserved: a system profile (the factory declares no .WithSystem(),
which defaults to kNone) and a guest's ORIGINAL profile (.WithGuest is
kOffTheRecordOnly). Atrium's per-space profiles are neither - they come from
ProfileManager::GetProfileByPath on user_data_dir subdirectories, which are
regular - so the identity is exactly the missing piece.

Both guards now log the profile's path and its otr/guest/system/regular flags.
One reproduction turns "unknown" into "named", instead of a fourth theory.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../render_view_context_menu.cc               | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
index d6e2c8870fb88..c65527f7da9b0 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
@@ -2892,6 +2892,21 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::AppendSearchProvider() {
   AutocompleteClassifier* const classifier =
       AutocompleteClassifierFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile());
   if (!classifier) {
+    // GetForProfile passes create=true, so null means the factory's
+    // ProfileSelections declined this profile TYPE, not that the service was
+    // merely absent. Both unserved types are reachable in principle - a system
+    // profile (no .WithSystem(), which defaults to kNone) and a guest's
+    // original profile (.WithGuest(kOffTheRecordOnly)) - and Atrium's own
+    // per-space profiles are none of those, so the identity is the missing
+    // fact. Logged rather than guessed at: one reproduction names it.
+    Profile* const profile = GetProfile();
+    LOG(ERROR) << "Atrium: no AutocompleteClassifier for profile"
+               << " path=" << (profile ? profile->GetPath().BaseName().value()
+                                       : "<null profile>")
+               << " otr=" << (profile && profile->IsOffTheRecord())
+               << " guest=" << (profile && profile->IsGuestSession())
+               << " system=" << (profile && profile->IsSystemProfile())
+               << " regular=" << (profile && profile->IsRegularProfile());
     return;
   }
 
@@ -2913,6 +2928,13 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::AppendSearchProvider() {
     TemplateURLService* const template_urls =
         TemplateURLServiceFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile());
     if (!template_urls) {
+      Profile* const profile = GetProfile();
+      LOG(ERROR) << "Atrium: no TemplateURLService for profile"
+                 << " path=" << (profile ? profile->GetPath().BaseName().value()
+                                         : "<null profile>")
+                 << " otr=" << (profile && profile->IsOffTheRecord())
+                 << " guest=" << (profile && profile->IsGuestSession())
+                 << " system=" << (profile && profile->IsSystemProfile());
       return;
     }
     const TemplateURL* const default_provider =
